      "id": "summary",
      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Despite a long absence from parliament, Burnham showed he could hold his own and, despite some nerves, even enjoy himself</p><p>The coming months will show whether Andy Burnham fits Kemi Badenoch’s charge of a leader too obsessed with being liked to make hard choices. One thing, however, does seem clear from his first outing at prime minister’s questions: he likes saying yes.</p><p>The very first question came from a political opponent – Ann Davies of Plaid Cymru – but Burnham replied as if she was a valued constituent, saying he understood her worries about <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/aug/30/pc-harper-killers-prison-early-release-scheme\">the prison early release scheme</a> and hoped she could be reassured.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/02/burnhams-first-pmqs-showed-a-leader-who-wants-to-please-but-knows-how-to-push-back\">Continue reading...</a>"
